[agent] **Handling the overlapping exports:** The two exports together held 680 rows with 80 byte-identical re-delivered rows (`transactions_export_2.csv` re-delivers the tail of file 1). I confirmed the overlap was non-conflicting (600 distinct full rows == 600 distinct `row_id`s, no `row_id` mapped to two different rows), then loaded the canonical 600-row union.
[agent] **One correction during the run:** My first load fed the full 680-row union and relied on primary-key upsert to dedupe. The CLI's offline insert *appends* (the readback showed 680 rows / 80 duplicate `row_id`s) — it does not upsert or dedupe within a batch on the offline store. So I deleted and recreated the feature group and reloaded the pre-deduplicated 600-row dataset, giving exactly-once semantics in both stores.
[agent] Note on the interface: `hops fg insert` is append-only on the offline store with no exposed write-operation/upsert flag, so the caller must deduplicate by record key before ingestion — the CLI won't enforce one-row-per-key on the offline side at write time (the online store does upsert on the key).
